/*Q17. In an examination, Dev is asked to check whether the string comprises only digits. If the string contains only digits, print “<String> has
only digits”, else print “<String> doesn't have only digits”. Can you clear this exam by writing a Java program for it?
Input format:
• Asingle line containing a string str.
Output format:
• If the string contains only digits, print: "<str> has only digits" (where str is the input string).
• If the string contains any non-digit character, print: "<str> doesn't have only digits".
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class OnlyDigits {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String str = sc.nextLine();
        boolean onlyDigits = !str.isEmpty();
        for (char c : str.toCharArray()) {
            if (!Character.isDigit(c)) {
                onlyDigits = false;
                break;
            }
        }
        if (onlyDigits) System.out.println(str + " has only digits");
        else System.out.println(str + " doesn't have only digits");
        sc.close();
    }
}
